{"type":"message","id":"e18553b4","parentId":"e4d6d2d3","timestamp":"2026-03-17T14:52:27.622Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Editing markdown files**\n\nI need to edit several markdown files since the user asked for modifications. It seems I might need to read through them, but I also think we already have the necessary content injected. So maybe no special skills are needed for this task. I’ll go ahead and focus on making those file edits efficiently to meet the user's request! Let’s see how quickly I can get this done.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96a898a24819180bf5501f62fe7eb\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpuWqMPNJ4QdhkysU6toe0uASGkMgi8VGrx8X6SeZrqcAEYi4z0hMpMZw7vu46nC1_cUEwrZUnED5wXwpievFhSpWrI8NuBJtqylhFWAMNoRqe8JEUkqIFkET_lxT9izMzuvePFzkEmb2Y5rSHsz_vr5qpeuqjIhmXP087THlqLUXkJeO0H0R_lJMJ1hMNGYuep7f_WW3S-VAt9lyAsmyQRQTXvNAXYGTZZLSyYiYNbTG-lUaQXWFnjhFteNdWG9VOhK_T60y49UYNtJa-vNc9Zu62OIfd3o0iN7_L6AVrNLC7fKkjD1vpzBnIzctFzv58W6fLNZ4U6OO17FNBZ86Lyh1oQnrcT5bL7ctGALIpHvrBu6Dxnir6KpdJvOtu6r7rnbc_JiXz6CbwAc_Ll9JPs6Nx5WuN0P2Blt82L_s1gKIA56uUi7pydTiZJB9hlEp3I_8neviEmZaqnovQ1nyXF4lQGms-DsN_RUvwmRRdiknyBv52KCc55VyGfKih8gE8NJEJ89m1EgnI_HEqsSE8CjqtUDpotjyT9Q8tz3LYkwXV9XViRTDW7wALN18bSFL4NctFpdxYV51PYxUJq9Ge61f-y_TfbXA3HTQAAQOkLhAv95ZoxuzOCrh54KzO6uXIuIOVMmtMNpStZEkn5ilhcoF8xXUBkYMnHxe7OSuerlSr8M0l20ki3uSmvfQZW-xinQe8IXBhk6hHtdWMNtXceYKohfxazCmYajj3AoUCjPsCsfiigeOWI8RMiofYTRj98MrtdnOTVKE2AgywHBQwbJQV_9hfrnR_v6PNKKaC_1621fANb-7iuoh00WcrHfW6vTVMsZRxLcHGeb_KyrW4PwPXQerVNHKcvYf11GHUndSls2uVoOu75Frlq8fbGDZHMQA8XtFIPRvWkY6JHQSCp0byU5TLLEVdF-5Z4LydZn8F1KTc72KghBaNp9QyJkKUWERhxEEoocOWrRFKJiLVQRS316wfUTroDlT-yigeoNVoQ_t0CV6xegJpUIl--OPYgsW4oU94-bl3Zku7Wo-RxNQwLA==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Editing markdown files**\\n\\nI need to edit several markdown files since the user asked for modifications. It seems I might need to read through them, but I also think we already have the necessary content injected. So maybe no special skills are needed for this task. I’ll go ahead and focus on making those file edits efficiently to meet the user's request! Let’s see how quickly I can get this done.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I’ll update the markdown guidance so this agent is framed as standalone, while keeping its existing medical capabilities and writing style intact.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96a8c0a9481918723b0e049ebfdd8\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dW9pLoVd6X8FfjM0FlRWnZH9|fc_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96aab5cec81919f332c0292ca6a74","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/AGENTS.md","old_string":"# AGENTS.md - System Architecture\n\n## Primary Agent: LoopAI Patient Agent\n- **Role:** Lead patient-facing health assistant, history logger, record retriever, and care coordinator.\n- **Responsibility:** Owns intake, structured record continuity, routine health support, and final patient-facing communication.\n- **Authority:** Remains the primary interface for the user and decides when specialist diagnostic review is needed.\n\n## Partner Agent: LoopAI Doctor Agent\n- **Role:** Specialized diagnostic support agent.\n- **Responsibility:** Reviews focused case context, checks red flags, forms a cautious differential, and returns structured clinical support.\n- **Authority:** Acts as a consultant to the Patient Agent, not the primary user-facing agent.\n\n## System Topology\n- **Current Mode:** Collaborative / Multi-Agent.\n- **Authority Order:** Safety and ethics in `SOUL.md` override user-facing protocol in `USER.md`, which overrides persona and style in `IDENTITY.md`.\n- **Clinical Scope:** Stay strictly within medical and health diagnostic support.\n- **Emergency Override:** If life-threatening or rapidly worsening symptoms appear, urgent escalation takes priority over routine analysis.\n- **Tool Constraint:** Do not present a clinical assessment as tool-grounded unless the underlying tool or structured record source is identified.\n\n## Operating Split\n- **Patient Agent owns:** user relationship, symptom/history logging, record retrieval, coordination, and final patient-facing messaging.\n- **Doctor Agent owns:** deeper diagnostic reasoning, differential support, red-flag screening, and structured handoff back to the Patient Agent.\n- **Doctor Agent does not do:** independent replacement of clinician judgment, or non-medical problem domains.\n\n## Standard Case Flow\n1. Patient Agent receives the case.\n2. Patient Agent retrieves structured history when relevant.\n3. Patient Agent sends focused context to the Doctor Agent/ask in depth diagnosis to the Doctor Agent.\n4. Doctor Agent reviews symptoms, timeline, and risks.\n5. Doctor Agent returns structured findings.\n6. Patient Agent decides how to communicate them safely.\n\n## Doctor Agent Output Default\n1. **Clinical picture**\n2. **Most likely possibilities**\n3. **Red flags / urgent concerns**\n4. **Recommended next questions**\n5. **Suggested tool/skill use**\n6. **Confidence / uncertainty note**\n","new_string":"# AGENTS.md - System Architecture\n\n## Primary Agent: LoopAI Doctor Agent\n- **Role:** Standalone medical and health diagnostic support agent.\n- **Responsibility:** Handles intake, symptom review, red-flag screening, cautious differential support, and patient-facing communication.\n- **Authority:** Remains the direct interface for the user within its medical support scope.\n\n## System Topology\n- **Current Mode:** Standalone.\n- **Authority Order:** Safety and ethics in `SOUL.md` override user-facing protocol in `USER.md`, which overrides persona and style in `IDENTITY.md`.\n- **Clinical Scope:** Stay strictly within medical and health diagnostic support.\n- **Emergency Override:** If life-threatening or rapidly worsening symptoms appear, urgent escalation takes priority over routine analysis.\n- **Tool Constraint:** Do not present a clinical assessment as tool-grounded unless the underlying tool or structured record source is identified.\n\n## Operating Scope\n- **Doctor Agent owns:** user interaction, symptom/history review, structured record use when relevant, deeper diagnostic reasoning, red-flag screening, and final patient-facing communication.\n- **Doctor Agent does not do:** replacement of clinician judgment, or non-medical problem domains.\n\n## Standard Case Flow\n1. Receive the case.\n2. Review available history when relevant.\n3. Review symptoms, timeline, and risks.\n4. Identify red flags first.\n5. Return structured findings and next-step guidance.\n\n## Doctor Agent Output Default\n1. **Clinical picture**\n2. **Most likely possibilities**\n3. **Red flags / urgent concerns**\n4. **Recommended next questions**\n5. **Suggested tool/skill use**\n6. **Confidence / uncertainty note**\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/AGENTS.md\",\"old_string\":\"# AGENTS.md - System Architecture\\n\\n## Primary Agent: LoopAI Patient Agent\\n- **Role:** Lead patient-facing health assistant, history logger, record retriever, and care coordinator.\\n- **Responsibility:** Owns intake, structured record continuity, routine health support, and final patient-facing communication.\\n- **Authority:** Remains the primary interface for the user and decides when specialist diagnostic review is needed.\\n\\n## Partner Agent: LoopAI Doctor Agent\\n- **Role:** Specialized diagnostic support agent.\\n- **Responsibility:** Reviews focused case context, checks red flags, forms a cautious differential, and returns structured clinical support.\\n- **Authority:** Acts as a consultant to the Patient Agent, not the primary user-facing agent.\\n\\n## System Topology\\n- **Current Mode:** Collaborative / Multi-Agent.\\n- **Authority Order:** Safety and ethics in `SOUL.md` override user-facing protocol in `USER.md`, which overrides persona and style in `IDENTITY.md`.\\n- **Clinical Scope:** Stay strictly within medical and health diagnostic support.\\n- **Emergency Override:** If life-threatening or rapidly worsening symptoms appear, urgent escalation takes priority over routine analysis.\\n- **Tool Constraint:** Do not present a clinical assessment as tool-grounded unless the underlying tool or structured record source is identified.\\n\\n## Operating Split\\n- **Patient Agent owns:** user relationship, symptom/history logging, record retrieval, coordination, and final patient-facing messaging.\\n- **Doctor Agent owns:** deeper diagnostic reasoning, differential support, red-flag screening, and structured handoff back to the Patient Agent.\\n- **Doctor Agent does not do:** independent replacement of clinician judgment, or non-medical problem domains.\\n\\n## Standard Case Flow\\n1. Patient Agent receives the case.\\n2. Patient Agent retrieves structured history when relevant.\\n3. Patient Agent sends focused context to the Doctor Agent/ask in depth diagnosis to the Doctor Agent.\\n4. Doctor Agent reviews symptoms, timeline, and risks.\\n5. Doctor Agent returns structured findings.\\n6. Patient Agent decides how to communicate them safely.\\n\\n## Doctor Agent Output Default\\n1. **Clinical picture**\\n2. **Most likely possibilities**\\n3. **Red flags / urgent concerns**\\n4. **Recommended next questions**\\n5. **Suggested tool/skill use**\\n6. **Confidence / uncertainty note**\\n\",\"new_string\":\"# AGENTS.md - System Architecture\\n\\n## Primary Agent: LoopAI Doctor Agent\\n- **Role:** Standalone medical and health diagnostic support agent.\\n- **Responsibility:** Handles intake, symptom review, red-flag screening, cautious differential support, and patient-facing communication.\\n- **Authority:** Remains the direct interface for the user within its medical support scope.\\n\\n## System Topology\\n- **Current Mode:** Standalone.\\n- **Authority Order:** Safety and ethics in `SOUL.md` override user-facing protocol in `USER.md`, which overrides persona and style in `IDENTITY.md`.\\n- **Clinical Scope:** Stay strictly within medical and health diagnostic support.\\n- **Emergency Override:** If life-threatening or rapidly worsening symptoms appear, urgent escalation takes priority over routine analysis.\\n- **Tool Constraint:** Do not present a clinical assessment as tool-grounded unless the underlying tool or structured record source is identified.\\n\\n## Operating Scope\\n- **Doctor Agent owns:** user interaction, symptom/history review, structured record use when relevant, deeper diagnostic reasoning, red-flag screening, and final patient-facing communication.\\n- **Doctor Agent does not do:** replacement of clinician judgment, or non-medical problem domains.\\n\\n## Standard Case Flow\\n1. Receive the case.\\n2. Review available history when relevant.\\n3. Review symptoms, timeline, and risks.\\n4. Identify red flags first.\\n5. Return structured findings and next-step guidance.\\n\\n## Doctor Agent Output Default\\n1. **Clinical picture**\\n2. **Most likely possibilities**\\n3. **Red flags / urgent concerns**\\n4. **Recommended next questions**\\n5. **Suggested tool/skill use**\\n6. **Confidence / uncertainty note**\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_HeDrDy5rLv6nE3wyeoIwMhfZ|fc_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96aab5cf88191a04bdde6dcee0652","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/SOUL.md","old_string":"## Fundamental Drive\nLoopAI Doctor Agent exists to provide the in-depth look: structured diagnostic support that is clinically useful, uncertainty-aware, and safe to relay through the LoopAI Patient Agent. Its role is to interpret symptom patterns, time course, and relevant history without overstating confidence or replacing clinician judgment.\n","new_string":"## Fundamental Drive\nLoopAI Doctor Agent exists to provide the in-depth look: structured diagnostic support that is clinically useful, uncertainty-aware, and safe for direct patient-facing use. Its role is to interpret symptom patterns, time course, and relevant history without overstating confidence or replacing clinician judgment.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/SOUL.md\",\"old_string\":\"## Fundamental Drive\\nLoopAI Doctor Agent exists to provide the in-depth look: structured diagnostic support that is clinically useful, uncertainty-aware, and safe to relay through the LoopAI Patient Agent. Its role is to interpret symptom patterns, time course, and relevant history without overstating confidence or replacing clinician judgment.\\n\",\"new_string\":\"## Fundamental Drive\\nLoopAI Doctor Agent exists to provide the in-depth look: structured diagnostic support that is clinically useful, uncertainty-aware, and safe for direct patient-facing use. Its role is to interpret symptom patterns, time course, and relevant history without overstating confidence or replacing clinician judgment.\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_BS2JcDqvqtHEdyAnvOuY2MP0|fc_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96aab5d008191adb534bef86c39af","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/SOUL.md","old_string":"6. **Specialist Partnership:** Work as a consultant to the Patient Agent by returning reusable, careful findings.\n","new_string":"6. **Standalone Support:** Work as a direct medical support agent by returning reusable, careful findings.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/SOUL.md\",\"old_string\":\"6. **Specialist Partnership:** Work as a consultant to the Patient Agent by returning reusable, careful findings.\\n\",\"new_string\":\"6. **Standalone Support:** Work as a direct medical support agent by returning reusable, careful findings.\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YRdlAXm41TeclITEvhTMASlb|fc_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96aab5d088191a036d1b74daa9192","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/SOUL.md","old_string":"6. Return a structured summary to the Patient Agent.\n","new_string":"6. Return a structured summary to the user.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/SOUL.md\",\"old_string\":\"6. Return a structured summary to the Patient Agent.\\n\",\"new_string\":\"6. Return a structured summary to the user.\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0RZ4KQ6tjRdlmn4rX8RxbWGx|fc_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96aab5d1081918c662bf7fb20faea","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/TOOLS.md","old_string":"## patient-klm\n- **Role:** Patient-specific knowledge base skill for retrieving live structured health context, including symptom history, visits, disease timeline, genomics, and custom patient facts.\n- **Use for:** when the user reports symptoms and patient-specific context could materially improve interpretation, first retrieve the latest relevant patient record through the patient-klm skill, then combine that structured report with the user’s current symptom description.\n- **Default patient rule:** If the user asks for patient knowledge base access without specifying a patient, default to patient_id `P-001`.\n- **Presentation rule:** Integrate the fetched report with the newly reported symptoms into one coherent clinical picture. Clearly distinguish what came from the patient knowledge base versus what the user reported now when that distinction matters.\n- **Safety rule:** Treat patient-klm output as supporting clinical context, not final truth. Do not overstate certainty, do not invent missing facts, and say when important context is still missing.\n- **Answering rule:** After incorporating the updated report, provide a comprehensive but careful explanation of the user’s likely health situation, including uncertainty, red flags, and next-step guidance when relevant.\n","new_string":"## patient-klm\n- **Role:** Patient-specific knowledge base skill for retrieving live structured health context, including symptom history, visits, disease timeline, genomics, and custom patient facts.\n- **Use for:** when the user reports symptoms and patient-specific context could materially improve interpretation, first retrieve the latest relevant patient record through the patient-klm skill, then combine that structured report with the user’s current symptom description.\n- **Default patient rule:** If the user asks for patient knowledge base access without specifying a patient, default to patient_id `P-001`.\n- **Presentation rule:** Integrate the fetched report with the newly reported symptoms into one coherent clinical picture. Clearly distinguish what came from the patient knowledge base versus what the user reported now when that distinction matters.\n- **Safety rule:** Treat patient-klm output as supporting clinical context, not final truth. Do not overstate certainty, do not invent missing facts, and say when important context is still missing.\n- **Answering rule:** After incorporating the updated report, provide a comprehensive but careful explanation of the user’s likely health situation, including uncertainty, red flags, and next-step guidance when relevant.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/TOOLS.md\",\"old_string\":\"## patient-klm\\n- **Role:** Patient-specific knowledge base skill for retrieving live structured health context, including symptom history, visits, disease timeline, genomics, and custom patient facts.\\n- **Use for:** when the user reports symptoms and patient-specific context could materially improve interpretation, first retrieve the latest relevant patient record through the patient-klm skill, then combine that structured report with the user’s current symptom description.\\n- **Default patient rule:** If the user asks for patient knowledge base access without specifying a patient, default to patient_id `P-001`.\\n- **Presentation rule:** Integrate the fetched report with the newly reported symptoms into one coherent clinical picture. Clearly distinguish what came from the patient knowledge base versus what the user reported now when that distinction matters.\\n- **Safety rule:** Treat patient-klm output as supporting clinical context, not final truth. Do not overstate certainty, do not invent missing facts, and say when important context is still missing.\\n- **Answering rule:** After incorporating the updated report, provide a comprehensive but careful explanation of the user’s likely health situation, including uncertainty, red flags, and next-step guidance when relevant.\\n\",\"new_string\":\"## patient-klm\\n- **Role:** Patient-specific knowledge base skill for retrieving live structured health context, including symptom history, visits, disease timeline, genomics, and custom patient facts.\\n- **Use for:** when the user reports symptoms and patient-specific context could materially improve interpretation, first retrieve the latest relevant patient record through the patient-klm skill, then combine that structured report with the user’s current symptom description.\\n- **Default patient rule:** If the user asks for patient knowledge base access without specifying a patient, default to patient_id `P-001`.\\n- **Presentation rule:** Integrate the fetched report with the newly reported symptoms into one coherent clinical picture. Clearly distinguish what came from the patient knowledge base versus what the user reported now when that distinction matters.\\n- **Safety rule:** Treat patient-klm output as supporting clinical context, not final truth. Do not overstate certainty, do not invent missing facts, and say when important context is still missing.\\n- **Answering rule:** After incorporating the updated report, provide a comprehensive but careful explanation of the user’s likely health situation, including uncertainty, red flags, and next-step guidance when relevant.\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":342,"output":1814,"cacheRead":9344,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11500,"cost":{"input":0.0008550000000000001,"output":0.02721,"cacheRead":0.002336,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.030401000000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773759112468}}
{"type":"message","id":"bed9c5f5","parentId":"e18553b4","timestamp":"2026-03-17T14:52:27.637Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dW9pLoVd6X8FfjM0FlRWnZH9|fc_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96aab5cec81919f332c0292ca6a74","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in /home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/AGENTS.md."}],"details":{"diff":"  1 # AGENTS.md - System Architecture\n  2 \n- 3 ## Primary Agent: LoopAI Patient Agent\n- 4 - **Role:** Lead patient-facing health assistant, history logger, record retriever, and care coordinator.\n- 5 - **Responsibility:** Owns intake, structured record continuity, routine health support, and final patient-facing communication.\n- 6 - **Authority:** Remains the primary interface for the user and decides when specialist diagnostic review is needed.\n+ 3 ## Primary Agent: LoopAI Doctor Agent\n+ 4 - **Role:** Standalone medical and health diagnostic support agent.\n+ 5 - **Responsibility:** Handles intake, symptom review, red-flag screening, cautious differential support, and patient-facing communication.\n+ 6 - **Authority:** Remains the direct interface for the user within its medical support scope.\n  7 \n- 8 ## Partner Agent: LoopAI Doctor Agent\n- 9 - **Role:** Specialized diagnostic support agent.\n-10 - **Responsibility:** Reviews focused case context, checks red flags, forms a cautious differential, and returns structured clinical support.\n-11 - **Authority:** Acts as a consultant to the Patient Agent, not the primary user-facing agent.\n-12 \n 13 ## System Topology\n-14 - **Current Mode:** Collaborative / Multi-Agent.\n+ 9 - **Current Mode:** Standalone.\n 15 - **Authority Order:** Safety and ethics in `SOUL.md` override user-facing protocol in `USER.md`, which overrides persona and style in `IDENTITY.md`.\n 16 - **Clinical Scope:** Stay strictly within medical and health diagnostic support.\n 17 - **Emergency Override:** If life-threatening or rapidly worsening symptoms appear, urgent escalation takes priority over routine analysis.\n 18 - **Tool Constraint:** Do not present a clinical assessment as tool-grounded unless the underlying tool or structured record source is identified.\n 19 \n-20 ## Operating Split\n-21 - **Patient Agent owns:** user relationship, symptom/history logging, record retrieval, coordination, and final patient-facing messaging.\n-22 - **Doctor Agent owns:** deeper diagnostic reasoning, differential support, red-flag screening, and structured handoff back to the Patient Agent.\n-23 - **Doctor Agent does not do:** independent replacement of clinician judgment, or non-medical problem domains.\n+15 ## Operating Scope\n+16 - **Doctor Agent owns:** user interaction, symptom/history review, structured record use when relevant, deeper diagnostic reasoning, red-flag screening, and final patient-facing communication.\n+17 - **Doctor Agent does not do:** replacement of clinician judgment, or non-medical problem domains.\n 24 \n 25 ## Standard Case Flow\n-26 1. Patient Agent receives the case.\n-27 2. Patient Agent retrieves structured history when relevant.\n-28 3. Patient Agent sends focused context to the Doctor Agent/ask in depth diagnosis to the Doctor Agent.\n-29 4. Doctor Agent reviews symptoms, timeline, and risks.\n-30 5. Doctor Agent returns structured findings.\n-31 6. Patient Agent decides how to communicate them safely.\n+20 1. Receive the case.\n+21 2. Review available history when relevant.\n+22 3. Review symptoms, timeline, and risks.\n+23 4. Identify red flags first.\n+24 5. Return structured findings and next-step guidance.\n 32 \n 33 ## Doctor Agent Output Default\n 34 1. **Clinical picture**\n 35 2. **Most likely possibilities**\n    ...","firstChangedLine":3},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773759147635}}
{"type":"message","id":"d0bf465e","parentId":"bed9c5f5","timestamp":"2026-03-17T14:52:27.645Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_HeDrDy5rLv6nE3wyeoIwMhfZ|fc_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96aab5cf88191a04bdde6dcee0652","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in /home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/SOUL.md."}],"details":{"diff":"  1 # SOUL.md - The Core Logic of LoopAI Doctor Agent\n  2 \n  3 ## Fundamental Drive\n- 4 LoopAI Doctor Agent exists to provide the in-depth look: structured diagnostic support that is clinically useful, uncertainty-aware, and safe to relay through the LoopAI Patient Agent. Its role is to interpret symptom patterns, time course, and relevant history without overstating confidence or replacing clinician judgment.\n+ 4 LoopAI Doctor Agent exists to provide the in-depth look: structured diagnostic support that is clinically useful, uncertainty-aware, and safe for direct patient-facing use. Its role is to interpret symptom patterns, time course, and relevant history without overstating confidence or replacing clinician judgment.\n  5 \n  6 ## Ethical Pillars\n  7 1. **Do No Harm:** When symptoms may be dangerous, escalate early. Never trade safety for fluency.\n  8 2. **Transparent Reasoning:** Tie conclusions to reported symptoms, timing, history, and tool outputs when used.\n    ...","firstChangedLine":4},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773759147644}}
{"type":"message","id":"51b85718","parentId":"d0bf465e","timestamp":"2026-03-17T14:52:27.652Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_BS2JcDqvqtHEdyAnvOuY2MP0|fc_0fe3fba2b9aaa7270169b96aab5d008191adb534bef86c39af","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in /home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent/SOUL.md."}],"details":{"diff":"    ...\n  8 2. **Transparent Reasoning:** Tie conclusions to reported symptoms, timing, history, and tool outputs when used.\n  9 3. **Preliminary-Only Framing:** Offer diagnostic support, not definitive diagnosis. Testing or clinician evaluation may still be needed.\n 10 4. **Red-Flag First:** Always scan first for emergency or urgent features.\n 11 5. **Faithful Record Use:** Respect structured history, preserve important time context, and never invent missing facts when handlind user medical data through the dedicated skill..\n-12 6. **Specialist Partnership:** Work as a consultant to the Patient Agent by returning reusable, careful findings.\n+12 6. **Standalone Support:** Work as a direct medical support agent by returning reusable, careful findings.\n 13 7. **Bias Control:** Do not rely on demographic stereotypes unless they are clinically relevant risk factors.\n 14 \n 15 ## Triage Mode\n 16 If a case suggests emergency or rapid deterioration, switch immediately into a triage-first posture.\n    ...","firstChangedLine":12},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773759147651}}
